Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:05:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 164/167] hjviewer: pinned builds offer no button to RustDesk's
 pages

A message box showed upstream's [JumpLink] wherever its message had a
link: the core's and a peer's messages link only to RustDesk's docs on
rustdesk.com (HELPER_URL for a peer's message, the Wayland login screen and
the X11 requirement for a refused login). The Wayland keyboard prompt's
"Why this happens" opened an issue on RustDesk's GitHub. A pinned build is
not RustDesk's app and shows neither button now, as it shows no "Powered by
RustDesk"; it tells by the links' pinned-server flag (allow-deep-link-
password pinned to N), which also keeps it to hjviewer:// links. Any other
build keeps upstream's buttons, and a message without a link asks the
core nothing, as before.

The other ways to RustDesk's pages were closed in pinned builds already:
"Powered by RustDesk" (hide-powered-by-me), the public server's pricing
link (a pinned build has its own server), upstream's update cards and
changelog (a custom client checks no RustDesk release), and links inside
a message's text (hjvLinksOff in a build with update keys). The help cards
of macOS and Linux keep their docs links; no pinned build is made for
either. The About screens, the installer's licence and the wake guide link
to this project's repository, the source the AGPL offers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
